Package: timeledger
Type: Package
Title: Auditable Time Accounting for Evaluating Continuous Event Detectors
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Tejas", "Menneni", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    email = "maintainer@example.org")
Description: Evaluates detectors of events in long continuous recordings,
    such as atrial fibrillation monitors, when detectors cover different
    parts of a recording, abstain, lose their input, or split one true event
    into several alarms. All inputs are reduced to one table of disjoint
    half-open time intervals per record that states the reference rhythm,
    whether input was available, and what each detector answered. Every
    reported quantity (answer coverage, sensitivity on answered time,
    full-period capture, episode detection under a named matching rule,
    false-alarm burden and event burden with bounds for incomplete
    predictions) is a sum over that table, reported with its numerator,
    denominator and excluded time, and traceable to the intervals behind it.
    Includes an exact one-to-one episode matching rule, paired comparisons
    on own, shared and full time, a subject-level cluster bootstrap, a
    base-R reader and writer for 'WFDB' annotation files, and a
    compatibility mode that reproduces the atrial fibrillation statistics of
    the 'WFDB' program 'epicmp' (Moody 2020,
    <https://physionet.org/content/wfdb/10.7.0/>).
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
